# GTA916 Conventions

GTA916 is a Sacramento (916)-themed FiveM roleplay server plus content
channels (faceless YouTube, streaming, marketing). Umbrella plan:
`docs/strategy/gta916-roadmap-whitepaper.md`. Public soft launch target:
mid-October 2026.

## Platform

- Target platform is **FiveM for GTAV Enhanced** (early access). Server
  component is "Cfx Server", runtime lives at `~/gta916/server-enhanced` +
  `~/gta916/txData-enhanced`. Legacy runtime (`~/gta916/server`, `~/gta916/txData`)
  is a fallback only. Both share ports 30120/40120 - never run both.
- Enhanced quirks and fixes: `docs/setup/gtav-enhanced.md`. Check it before
  debugging startup errors.

## Non-negotiables

- **Secrets never enter the repo.** Real keys go in runtime
  `server.cfg.local` (gitignored). Templates use `REPLACE_WITH_*`
  placeholders. Pre-commit secret scan must stay installed.
- **Changelog every session.** Any meaningful change gets an entry in
  `CHANGELOG.md` (newest first, `## YYYY-MM-DD - title` format).
- **Smoke tests before declaring anything working:**
  `docs/setup/private-smoke-tests.md`.
- **Monetization is Tebex-only and never pay-to-win.** Check
  `docs/policy/monetization-readiness.md` before any store/monetization work.
- Custom gameplay logic goes in `resources/[gta916]/`, not in the `qb-core/`
  fork (keep it mergeable with upstream).

## Commit style

Short imperative subject, body explains why. Push after committing (the
repo is the single source of truth for operational knowledge).
